f 1074 "To find the reciprocal of $-21,$ we divide $1$ by $-21.$ So, we obtain \n\n$$\n1 \\div (-21) = -\\dfrac{1}{21}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133497 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12789" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133497 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{1}{10}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133497 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2132b7c8-2d11-51c8-a1e3-06bb59c08f84" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133497 #edb/ref 1074 "We flip the numerator and the denominator. So, the reciprocal of $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ is  $\\dfrac{10}{1} = 10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133498 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12790" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133498 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the reciprocal of $-2\\,\\dfrac{1}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e757528d-e87f-5739-85d4-0b35267db955" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133498 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we write the mixed number as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n-2\\,\\dfrac{1}{3}=-\\dfrac{2\\cdot 3+1}{3}=-\\dfrac{7}{3}\n$$\n\nThen, we flip the numerator and the denominator, keeping the negative sign. Therefore, the reciprocal of $-2\\,\\dfrac{1}{3}$ is $-\\dfrac{3}{7}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133499 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12791" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133499 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the reciprocal of $0.4?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133499 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c2a7d91-c840-5f6a-8e9d-d17673e8cb70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133499 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we must convert the decimal to a fraction. Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n0.4 = \\dfrac{4}{10} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}{2}}}{{\\color{red}{5}}}.\n$$\n\nNow, we flip the fraction, as before. So the reciprocal of $0.4$ is $\\dfrac{{\\color{red}{5}}}{{\\color{blue}{2}}} = 2.5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133958 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133958 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133958 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134142 #edb/ref 175